# OpenRouter Rules

OpenRouter is used **only** as an internal peak-hour fallback provider for DeepSeek models. It is not advertised as a user-selectable provider; Cursor aliases map to direct providers and the gateway reroutes to OpenRouter upstream IDs during peak hours.

## Models

| Upstream id                        | Fallback target | Size class |
| ---------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`  | small/flash     | small      |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`    | big/pro         | big        |

Peak reroute mapping (non-downgraded traffic only):
- `deepseek-v4-pro`, `glm-5.3`, `kimi-k3` → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`
- everything else (`deepseek-v4-flash`, `glm-4.7`, `kimi-k2.7-code`, `thaura`) → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`

All subagent/router downgrades, lane-full overflows, Z.AI 429-quota fallbacks, and the compression worker use `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731` regardless of the originally requested model.

## API key

- Key field: `openRouterKeyEncrypted` in `config.AppSettings`
- Set via: `discursive set --openrouter-key <key>` or `--openrouter-key` flag on `init`
- Retrieved via: `settings.GetOpenRouterKey(dataRoot)` in gateway/server.go
- OpenRouter is optional — if no key is configured, peak traffic falls through to the direct provider (pay peak), zero downtime

## Pricing (USD per 1M tokens)

Source: https://openrouter.ai/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731 ·
https://openrouter.ai/deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813 — OpenRouter flat **list**
rates. OpenRouter does not apply peak/off-peak pricing
(https://openrouter.ai/blog/insights/why-openrouter-for-deepseek/), so these
rates apply year-round.

| Model                              | Cache hit | Input | Output |
| ---------------------------------- | --------- | ----- | ------ |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`  | $0.014    | $0.065 | $0.14  |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`    | $0.022    | $0.66  | $1.98  |

Typical blended (OpenRouter weighted average) informational rates shown in dashboard/README:
- flash: $0.0476 in / $0.384 out
- pro: $0.2365 in / $3.174 out

## Sanitizer policy

Reuse `PolicyDeepSeek` for OpenRouter traffic — pass the `thinking` object through.

## Upstream config

| Item        | Value                          |
| ----------- | ------------------------------ |
| Default URL | `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` |

## Credits endpoint

`GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/credits` returns `data.total_credits` and `data.total_usage`. Remaining credits = `total_credits - total_usage`. The balance is returned as USD (not a credit count). The endpoint may require a management key; on 401/403 surface an error string in the UI tooltip.

